      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Financing a roof replacement in Utah typically ranges from $10,000 to $21,000 for asphalt shingles and $18,000 to $35,000 for metal roofing systems.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "$10,000 to $21,000 for asphalt shingles and $18,000 to $35,000 for metal roofing systems"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Common Financing & Payment Options in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Contractor Promotional Financing: Many Utah roofing companies offer $0 down options with promotional periods such as 0% APR for 6 to 12 months (or no interest/no payments for a set introductory term) on approved credit . Examples include Olympus Cove Roofing (6 months no interest) and Utah Roofing Pros.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Home Equity Loans or HELOCs: A Home Equity Line of Credit through local credit unions or banks allows you to borrow against your home equity at generally lower interest rates, as offered by regional providers like Red Fox Roofing .",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Red Fox Roofing",
                "link": "https://redfoxroofingutah.com/financing/"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Insurance Claims: If your roof suffered wind, hail, or winter storm damage, many Utah contractors (such as Dynamite Roofing or A1 Roofing Utah ) specialize in insurance claim assistance. In these cases, you may only be responsible for paying your out-of-pocket insurance deductible (often around $1,000 to $2,500) rather than financing the full cost.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Government Assistance: Low-income or rural homeowners may qualify for the USDA Single Family Housing Repair Loans and Grants, which offer funds up to $40,000 for loans or $10,000 for grants to address critical safety hazards like severe roof damage .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like to narrow this down, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Are you looking for contractor payment plans , or do you suspect storm/insurance damage?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What city or county in Utah is the home located in?"
          }
        ]
      }
